=== SFI (Single Feature Importance) vs MDI/MDA/SHAP (AFML ch.8) ===
cite: López de Prado AFML ch.8 — SFI avoids substitution by scoring one feature at a time
intuition: MDI/MDA/SHAP on correlated features split credit; SFI asks 'how good alone?'
SFI mean_daily_CS_RankIC (univariate ridge OOF on fold 2):
vol_5         0.024283
mom_20        0.018488
rank_mom20    0.018488
vol_20        0.018178
mom_20_dup    0.014532
mom_10       -0.014454
mom_1        -0.017818
mom_5        -0.022106
substitution story: MDI split mom_20 vs mom_20_dup; SFI mom_20=+0.0185 mom_20_dup=+0.0145 (near-equal alone → duplicates are substitutes, not two independent alphas)
chart /workspace/Quant-trading-learn/public/p5/sfi_importance.png

=== Localformer/Transformer foil (same purged protocol; NO 'DL wins' claim) ===
cite: Yang et al. Qlib arXiv:2009.11189; Vaswani et al. 2017 Attention; Qlib benchmarks list Localformer (Jiang et al.)
note: we do NOT re-train Qlib Localformer weights — this is a teaching FOIL with a tiny causal attention pooling head
optional control: Qlib Alpha158 Transformer/Localformer checkpoints under the SAME anti-leakage protocol
attn_pool_ridge mean_CS_IC=-0.0103 t=-1.94 net_SR=-3.748 turn=1.6008 DSR=0.000
compare ridge mean_CS_IC=+0.0398 gbm=+0.0336
teach: under the SAME purged protocol, a tiny attention foil does NOT automatically beat trees/linear — do not claim 'DL wins'. Qlib's published Localformer/Transformer numbers are OPTIONAL CONTROLS, not a license to skip purge/embargo or cost accounting.
